# A second hand-labelled sample of Markdown documents edges (#2): a bare
# lowercase word naming a nested declaration (a field, an rpc, a method,
# a .pxf block, an enum value, a column), the class where a word is most
# likely to be an ordinary word. 40 were drawn from the 77 such edges of
# the nine public repositories of markdown-sample.pxf on 2026-10-14, by
# TestDrawSamples, in the same way, and judged by reading the sentence.
# 32 of the 40 are right: 0.80, against 0.931 for documents edges overall.
#
# These are the edges the linker keeps: it already drops a bare word
# whose section does not name the declaration's parent. The sample this
# replaces was drawn on 2026-10-08, before that rule, from 281 edges of
# 16 repositories: 17 of 39 were right (0.44), and the rule kept 11 of
# the 17 and 1 of the 22 wrong. What the rule costs in right edges is not
# measured by this sample.

